{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The quick-bond glue and rectangular magnets felt useful for small repairs and workshop fixtures, extending the attachment options I already use with tape, hook-and-loop strips, and resin.",
    "Pegboard hooks fit my growing collection of tools and fasteners, because keeping those supplies organized would help with my ongoing projects."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The pressure gauge requires a specific pressure range and fitting, and I have no current project needing either; owning inspection and measuring tools does not make every measuring device useful to me.",
    "Floor cleaner, merchandise bags, and dental syringes address tasks I have not shown a need for, unlike the fabrication, fastening, and repair supplies I have been choosing."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The suggestions seemed to treat general workshop or commercial usefulness as enough, even when an item had no clear role in my current projects.",
    "My interest in fastener assortments seemed to lead to more similar assortments without enough consideration of the cotter pins and screws I already have."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent cotter-pin purchase makes another large assortment less useful right now; a related item can fit my interests without being something I need to buy again.",
    "Practical compatibility matters: I would need hooks that fit my pegboard, screw sizes missing from my supplies, and gloves suitable for the resin and adhesives I use."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my hands-on repair interests but missed the difference between useful additions, duplicate supplies, and tools for tasks I am not doing."
}"}
